# The git-tracked bead export (rosary-4ebf52) is a DERIVED, STRUCTURED file:
# one JSON record per line, id-sorted. Git's default text merge auto-merges it
# most of the time — the id sort keeps unrelated beads on distant lines — but a
# line-level 3-way merge doesn't know what a line MEANS, and can produce
# syntactically valid JSONL that is semantically wrong (the same bead id twice,
# or a stale record winning). Merge it by RECORD instead: a real 3-way decision
# per bead id, id-sorted output, and a loud conflict — never a silent discard —
# when both branches drove the same bead to different states.
#
# The driver DEFINITION lives in git config, not here — per gitattributes(5),
# this line only REFERENCES a driver by name. Config is per-clone and can't be
# committed, so every clone must install it:
#
#     rsry hooks install     # sets merge.beads-jsonl.{name,driver}
#     rsry hooks status      # reports whether it's configured
#
# Without that config git silently falls back to the default text merge, which
# is today's (adequate-but-unsound) behaviour — so an un-installed clone is
# degraded, not broken.
.beads/beads.jsonl merge=beads-jsonl
